From 57d605fb75e1f4ecb2693d36a7d195fd9f276d4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:29:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Share every work, from both of its sheets, with a proper
 preview (build 95 note 15)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

His word, 2026-11-13 about 07:50 UTC, with The Paschal Homily's two sheets:
"allow every single work to be sharable by adding a share button here and
here". His first screenshot was the contents (a work of one section: About
this book alone, and under it the empty list's border, a rule before
nothing); the second was ••• (Reader settings, Bookmark this section, About
this book, Search Purify).

Every work of the Fathers and every council's document now has Share in both:
- in the contents, under About this book, the work itself;
- in •••, beside the bookmark (before About this book and Search, the rows
  that open other sheets), the part being read: the work's page at #sN, the
  website's own address for it, in a work of more than one part.
The sheet's own row, the Share mark from components/ui/icons, the catalog's
common.share in every language; it reads from the right in Arabic and Urdu.
It shares by the app's one way (lib/share/shareOut.ts): the work's title and
its page on purifyapp.net, never the app's localhost, the address bar's query
or the reader's paragraph. Once shared the sheet closes; with no share sheet
the link is copied and the row says "Link copied".

The empty list is not drawn for a work of one section (51 of 249 works and
some councils' documents), and About this book's last rule goes when nothing
follows it (every council's document ended in one).

The preview: a work's page named nothing of its own, so every work shared
unfolded as Purify's home ("Purify, Orthodox prayer, calendar, and
Scripture", the home page's address and canonical). lib/seo/preview.ts gives
both work pages their title, description, own address and canonical, and the
cover's picture whole (a portrait icon as the small card), Purify's own card
where a work has none. The website's alone: an app's page carries its title.

lib/reading/__tests__/shareWork.test.ts: 10 of its tests fail on the old
sheets and pages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
